# Mobile web design — desktop isolation

VC Dekho uses **desktop-first CSS**. Desktop styles are the default; mobile is layered on top.

## Golden rule

**Never change desktop appearance.** All mweb redesign work goes inside `@media (max-width: …)` blocks only.

- Do **not** edit shared base selectors outside media queries unless fixing a bug that affects both (rare — ask first).
- Do **not** convert the codebase to mobile-first (`min-width` desktop overrides) in this phase.
- Do **not** change desktop HTML structure for mobile convenience; prefer CSS-only overrides or mobile-only elements hidden on desktop.

## Canonical breakpoints

Use only these tiers (align JS `matchMedia` with CSS):

| Tier | Query | Use for |
|------|--------|---------|
| Tablet | `max-width: 992px` | Scroll unlock, home/hero layout |
| Mobile | `max-width: 768px` | Nav drawer, touch targets, filter bar |
| Small phone | `max-width: 640px` | Directory cards, profile section heads |

Avoid introducing new breakpoint values (720, 860, 960, etc.) unless replacing an existing one in the same PR.

**Desktop floor:** treat **≥993px** as dweb for QA.

## Scoping overrides

Prefer page/body scoping inside mobile blocks so rules cannot leak:

```css
/* ✅ GOOD — scoped, max-width only */
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  body.inv-dir-page .inv-dir-header { … }
  body.inv-investor-profile .inv-profile-hero-row { … }
}

/* ❌ BAD — changes desktop base */
.inv-dir-header { padding: 0.5rem; }

/* ❌ BAD — unscoped global that affects dweb at wrong widths */
.inv-dir-header { display: block; }
```

Existing body classes: `inv-dir-page`, `inv-page`, `inv-investor-profile`, `inv-person-profile`, `home-page`, `scrollable-page`.

## Mobile-only markup

If adding HTML/JS for mobile:

- Hide on desktop: `@media (min-width: 993px) { .mweb-only { display: none !important; } }`
- Or use elements that only render meaningfully under `max-width` (e.g. drawer/backdrop already gated by CSS).

Prefix new mobile-only classes with `mweb-` when they have no desktop role.

## Files and workflow

- Edit split bundles: `css/base.css`, `css/hero.css`, `css/directory.css`, `css/ambient.css`, `css/blog.css`.
- If editing `style.css`, run `node scripts/split_css.js` afterward — do not let split files drift.
- Bump `?v=` on changed CSS bundles in HTML/SSR after deploy.
- Largest mweb surface: `css/directory.css` (directories + profiles).

## JS alignment

- Filter drawer / mobile labels: `matchMedia('(max-width: 768px)')` in `investors/investors.js`, `people/people.js`.
- Parallax off: `992px` in `app.js` — do not change without matching CSS.

## Before finishing any mweb change

1. Spot-check **dweb at 1280px+** (nav, directory table, profile hero, home).
2. Spot-check **mweb at 375px** (iPhone width).
3. Confirm no desktop selector was modified outside `@media (max-width: …)`.
